<title>POLAND: Polish new car sales up 28.7 pct in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Polish new car sales up 28.7 pct in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car sales in Poland grew by 28.7 percent in January-May against the same period last year to 215,774 units, an independent car market monitoring agency, Samar, said in a report on Friday.</p>
<p>Samar said sales of commercial vehicles rose 23.8 percent to 21,874 over the same period.</p>
<p>Fiat topped the list of passenger car makers with 73,953 units sold and a 34.3 percent market share.</p>
